UID:986a679b95cd9f3c@role-business-corporate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260911T162630Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Honoring the Victims and Survivors of the Sep
 tember 11 Attacks
DESCRIPTION:Hello\, this is Governor Janet Mills\, and thank you for liste
 ning.\nRobert and Jackie Norton's son was waiting for them in California 2
 5 years ago. He was about to get married\, but his parents\, a retired cou
 ple from Lubec\, never made it to the ceremony. Their plane\, American Air
 lines Flight 11\, hit the North Tower of the World Trade Center in a horri
 fic act of terrorism on September 11\, 2001.\nKatie Ward\, the sister of S
 tephen Ward\, said her brother couldn't wait to take over the big city whe
 n he moved to New York. A native of Gorham\, Maine\, Stephen had big plans
 \, and he encouraged everyone to go after what they wanted and live their 
 best lives. Stephen was working on the 101st floor of the North Tower at t
 he World Trade Center that fateful day.\nRobert Jalbert was raised in Lewi
 ston and lived in Swampscott\, Massachusetts\, when he boarded United Flig
 ht 175 for a business trip to California. People described him as an easyg
 oing guy\, a good friend\, and a proud father who went to church every Sun
 day and served as a Eucharistic Minister. His flight struck the South Towe
 r of the World Trade Center.\nAttorney Jim Roux of Portland\, someone who 
 loved hiking Mount Washington. He was also on United Flight 175. Through t
 his Saturday\, September 12th\, the summit of Mount Washington will be lit
  by two pillars of light that will be visible from 100 miles away to honor
  Jim Roux and the thousands of others whose lives were cut short that day.
 \nCommander Robert Schlegel was a devoted husband\, a decorated officer\, 
 and an avid ice hockey and football player. Originally from Gray\, Maine\,
  Commander Schlegel had been awarded the Purple Heart and other medals for
  his career-long service in the U.S. Navy. He had been promoted just a mon
 th before he boarded American Airlines Flight 77\, which was then flown in
 to the Pentagon\, killing all on board.\n25 years ago\, Maine and the nati
 on were forever changed by the September 11th terrorist attacks. On this s
 olemn anniversary\, I join the Maine people in p\nhttp://www.maine.gov/gov
 ernor/mills/news/radio_address/honoring-victims-and-survivors-september-11
 -attacks-2026-09-11
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/news/radio_address/honoring-victim
 s-and-survivors-september-11-attacks-2026-09-11
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
